WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.240
We've just got news of some more cut scenes
from IT, including an extended quarry scene

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.330
with a funny moment from Eddie and a creepy-sounding
Bar Mitzvah ceremony involving Stan.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.860
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm talking about several deleted

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.449
scenes likely to appear in the Director's
Cut that's just been announced for the new

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:19.010
IT movie.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:22.460
Director Andy Muschietti revealed that we
can look forward to around 15 minutes of extra

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.410
footage in his extended cut that will be appearing
on the Blu-ray release.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.800
Just before I jump in, quick warning that
I'll be discussing spoilers from the movie,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.180
so take care if you've not seen IT yet.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:37.050
Also keep watching for details on the winner
of my Pennywise Funko Pop giveaway.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.440
The first cut scene that Andy Muschietti revealed
in an interview with Yahoo Movies is where

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.110
Stan addresses the guests at his Bar Mitzvah
ceremony and "he delivers a speech [where

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.649
he basically blames] all the adults [in] Derry"
for the murders and disappearances in the

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.649
town.

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:54.700
Muschietti also said this deleted scene "has
a great resolution", which makes me wonder

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.390
whether it's because Pennywise or the creepy
woman who terrorised him previously suddenly

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:03.160
appears in the congregation at the synagogue
while he's giving his speech.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.189
If you remember, in the theatrical release,
Stan had his first encounter with IT at the

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:11.219
beginning of the movie via the creepy woman
who emerged from the painting at the synagogue

00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:13.219
where he was practising for his Bar Mitzvah.

00:01:13.219 --> 00:01:18.929
So, perhaps the evil entity IT makes an appearance
again to disrupt Stan's speech or turn the

00:01:18.929 --> 00:01:21.039
crowd at the synagogue against him.

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:25.960
IT is often present in Derry whenever a horrific
event is happening or about to happen.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.499
For example, there was the scene where Henry
Bowers and his gang were beating up Ben on

00:01:29.499 --> 00:01:33.049
the bridge and a pair of adults driving by,
just look away.

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:37.499
As they drive past, Pennywise's signature
balloon floats up inside the car, showing

00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:42.420
how IT is at work making people either blind
to the violence or just normalising it.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.869
I also wonder whether Stan's attempt to reveal
this truth about IT is the reason why Pennywise

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:51.439
specifically targets him later and tries to
eat him when the Losers go down into the sewers

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:52.549
to find Bev.

00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:54.929
Let me know if you've got any theories about
the scene.

00:01:54.929 --> 00:01:57.729
I certainly can't wait to see it in full on
the Blu-ray.

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:02.709
Muschietti has also revealed that he enjoys
filming alternate takes and on IT he gave

00:02:02.709 --> 00:02:05.819
the actors freedom to improvise during their
scenes.

00:02:05.819 --> 00:02:09.679
As an example of this, the director explained
that he filmed a really funny extended scene

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:13.770
of the moment where the Losers jump off the
cliff into the quarry water below.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:18.349
In the movie, Eddie, Ben, Bill, Stan and Richie
are standing on the cliff above the quarry,

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:23.019
having a spitting match, and arguing over
who should jump first, before Bev turns up

00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:24.870
and jumps in ahead of them all.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.599
In the extended scene, the moment was opened
up and, according to Muschietti, "after the

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:33.549
spitting contest it escalates into something
that is completely weird [… and] is so funny.

00:02:33.549 --> 00:02:37.280
Jack Grazer [who plays] Eddie […] does something
that is completely bonkers."

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.819
I wonder if this deleted moment will show
the boys taking their competitive natures

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:43.859
to even greater extremes than the spitting
contest.

00:02:43.859 --> 00:02:48.330
Or could an earlier script give a clue as
to what this deleted moment might be?

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:52.180
In that earlier screenplay, at this point
in the film Eddie worries about whether it's

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:56.110
safe for Ben to go in the water because of
his cuts and Ritchie tells him to shut up

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:00.359
and stop going on about grey water, which
is what Eddie had been unhappy about earlier

00:03:00.359 --> 00:03:01.799
in the movie when they were in the sewers.

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:06.370
So, I'm thinking that the extended joking
around by Eddie could riff on this, showing

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.769
an even more exaggerated side of his hypochondria.

00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:14.240
After all, it seems like Jack, who plays Eddie,
has a real flair for working in the moment,

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:19.349
as according to co-screenwriter Gary Dauberman,
that line where Eddie mistakes the word 'gazebo'

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:24.050
for 'placebo' was also something that just
happened on the day.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.730
According to producer Barbara Muschietti,
several scenes featuring Bill's parents were

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:32.120
also cut from the theatrical release, though
they'll likely appear on the DVD.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.760
In the final film, the scene where Bill has
made a model of the Derry sewers in the family

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.630
garage shows us that there's a conflict between
Bill and his father who's exasperated by his

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.670
son's belief that Georgie is still alive.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:46.799
However, further moments were deleted from
the movie that focused on the growing distance

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:51.200
between Bill and his parents after the traumatic
disappearance of Georgie.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.590
Speaking to Collider, producer Muschietti
said the cut scenes show Bill trying to make

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:59.139
their situation better but his parents are
just unable to cope.

00:03:59.139 --> 00:04:04.069
By the way, when I was reading an earlier
script for the movie, I noticed it included

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:08.099
a scene where Bill speaks to his parents about
planning their annual trip to Acadia National

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:12.269
Park, but neither his mother nor father can
face even thinking about something their missing

00:04:12.269 --> 00:04:17.060
child loved so much and they end up walking
away, leaving Bill alone in the room.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.699
So, I'm guessing this is the kind of scene
which Muschietti is referring to as having

00:04:20.699 --> 00:04:22.919
been given the chop from the theatrical release.

